  "security_implications": "This FSM controls when the CPU boot can continue out of reset, based on lifecycle state (RAW test RMA, DFT enable) and external halt/JTAG signals. The continue_cpu_boot_o.done signal is only asserted as MuBi4True after passing through lifecycle checks and optionally waiting for JTAG command. Bypassing these checks (due to invalid lifecycle signal encoding, FSM glitch, or stuck-in-wait) could allow unauthorized debug access in secure lifecycle states, exposing sensitive data or firmware. The error handler only sets a flag without recovery, potentially leaving the system in an insecure state if an illegal state is entered.",
